# Example --patterns file for hlse_core (roadmap P0-3).
#
# Use this to teach HLSE your organization's internal token formats
# without a rebuild:
#
#   hlse_core --patterns custom-patterns.example secret --stdin
#   hlse_core --patterns custom-patterns.example scan .
#
# Format: one directive per line. '#' comments and blank lines are ignored.
#
#   SECRET <prefix> <min_suffix> <charset> <score> <label...>
#
#   prefix      literal token prefix to search for (e.g. "ACME_KEY_")
#   min_suffix  minimum number of <charset>-valid characters required
#               immediately after the prefix
#   charset     one of: alnum | alnum_dash | hex | alpha | digit
#   score       0-100 risk score for this credential type
#   label       free text (may contain spaces) — the credential type name
#               shown in findings; runs to end of line
#
# A malformed line is skipped with a warning; the rest of the file still
# loads. Custom patterns use the exact same matching and
# placeholder/example-value suppression logic as HLSE's built-in table, and
# never affect --benchmark (F1 is computed without --patterns).

# ACME Corp internal API key: "ACME_KEY_" + 20+ alphanumeric chars
SECRET ACME_KEY_ 20 alnum 85 ACME Internal API Key

# ACME Corp internal service token: "acme-svc-" + 16+ hex chars
SECRET acme-svc- 16 hex 70 ACME Service Token

# ACME Corp legacy deploy token: "DEPLOY-" + 24+ chars (letters/digits/-/_)
SECRET DEPLOY- 24 alnum_dash 75 ACME Legacy Deploy Token
